Police who searched the properties of Andrew Mountbatten-Windsor as part of investigations into his links to the late sex offender Jeffrey Epstein have agreed the search warrants were unlawful, a London judge said Thursday. The 66-year-old younger brother of King Charles II was arrested on February 19 on suspicion of misconduct in public office.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b5d413a-c094-11f1-afb8-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26278279161771.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b5d413a-c094-11f1-afb8-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26278279161771.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ec3669a6-c320-11f1-9c1d-5564e18e22be</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 14:09:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b5d413a-c094-11f1-afb8-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26278279161771.jpg">©  Kirsty Wigglesworth, AP file photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>New Paris exhibition explores Ireland's housing crisis through contemporary art</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261008-new-paris-exhibition-explores-ireland-s-housing-crisis-through-contemporary-art</link><description>
Huge demonstrations have been held over the last few weeks in Spain over its housing crisis, but the issue is not restricted to Spain. Many other countries also have a huge problem with housing, including Ireland, with experts saying that for every street of 10 houses, the country actually needs 12. Now a new exhibition in Paris at the Irish Cultural Centre is trying to reflect the issue. In Perspective, we spoke to the museum's director and one of the artists taking part.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/477d6478-c31b-11f1-a419-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-13830491366ac7990734e0d4-77560906.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/477d6478-c31b-11f1-a419-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-13830491366ac7990734e0d4-77560906.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5640a08e-c315-11f1-8972-1196b899eff1</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 13:29:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Stuart NORVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Maricarmen, the 87-year-old woman whose eviction shook Spain, dies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-maricarmen-the-87-year-old-woman-whose-eviction-shook-spain-dies</link><description>
María del Carmen Abascal, the 87-year-old woman whose eviction from her longtime Madrid home sparked nationwide protests across Spain and unleashed a political crisis, died on Wednesday while hospitalised.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58b2a060-c30b-11f1-915d-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/mini-35.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58b2a060-c30b-11f1-915d-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/mini-35.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6faf851c-c30b-11f1-a865-3f79da3b2fc9</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 11:54:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Nobel Prize in Literature awarded to Canada’s Anne Carson</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-nobel-prize-in-literature-awarded-to-canada-anne-carson</link><description>
The Nobel Prize in Literature was awarded to Canadian poet and essayist Anne Carson on Thursday by the Swedish Academy in Stockholm. Toronto-born Carson, 76, draws from ancient Greek and Roman literature for her works blending elements of poetry, essay and fiction. She will receive 12 million Swedish kronor (about $1.2 million) alongside the prestigious award.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/753f7710-c308-11f1-ad69-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24326138762555.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/753f7710-c308-11f1-ad69-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24326138762555.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b8550d60-c2f6-11f1-8765-cfeb110a5623</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 11:04:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/753f7710-c308-11f1-ad69-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24326138762555.jpg">©  Andy Kropa, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>Evicted pensioner Maricarmen, symbol of Spain's housing crisis, dies at 87</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261008-evicted-pensioner-maricarmen-symbol-of-spain-s-housing-crisis-dies-at-87</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, October 8: Maricarmen, the evicted Spanish pensioner who became the face of Spain's housing crisis, dies in hospital. Also, France braces for "Act Four" of high school student protests against dilapidated schools and poor staff presence. Finally, actress Zendaya sparks a row over etiquette at Paris Fashion Week.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/558cc210-c2e0-11f1-8bbe-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-10-08T05-20-42-110Z.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/558cc210-c2e0-11f1-8bbe-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-10-08T05-20-42-110Z.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0a9ddac8-c2e0-11f1-89c2-ed80457c6312</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 10:35:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dheepthika LAURENT</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>More than 30 killed in Russian strike on buses in Ukraine's Kramatorsk as Kyiv targets data centre</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-russian-strike-buses-kills-at-least-12-ukraine-kramatorsk-kyiv-targets-data-centre</link><description>
At least 30 people were killed in a Russian strike on two buses in the Ukrainian city of Kramatorsk in the eastern Donetsk region on Thursday. Earlier, a drone hit a data centre belonging to Russian technology company Yandex, causing a fire. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6c0032e-c326-11f1-b98f-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T102931Z-790862490-RC2YYNAEAEKW-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KRAMATORSK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6c0032e-c326-11f1-b98f-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T102931Z-790862490-RC2YYNAEAEKW-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KRAMATORSK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8f362904-c2f7-11f1-8a43-13e6cde67276</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 10:08:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6c0032e-c326-11f1-b98f-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T102931Z-790862490-RC2YYNAEAEKW-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KRAMATORSK.jpg">© National Police of Ukraine via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Evicted pensioner who sparked Spain housing protests dies: tenant union</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/evicted-pensioner-who-sparked-spain-housing-protests-dies-tenant-union</link><description>
Maricarmen ​Abascal, the 87-year-old woman whose eviction sparked housing ​protests in Spain, has died, Madrid's tenants' union said on Wednesday. Abascal's eviction sparked a series of ​protests ‌across Spain in the past couple ⁠of weeks, including activists camping on one of Madrid's main ‌squares, and calls for tackling a ⁠mounting housing crisis. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8815cb7e-c28a-11f1-90c5-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-213834-214117-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8815cb7e-c28a-11f1-90c5-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-213834-214117-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8d09a0ba-c28a-11f1-81df-59aac4d2b4ca</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 20:14:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Evicted pensioner Maricarmen Abascal, heart of Spain's housing protests, dies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261007-evicted-pensioner-maricarmen-abascal-heart-of-spain-housing-protests-has-died</link><description>
Maricarmen ​Abascal, the 87-year-old woman whose eviction sparked housing ​protests in Spain, has died, Madrid's tenants' union said on Wednesday. Massive protests following Abascal's eviction spiralled into a political crisis, eventually leading Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez to call a snap election.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ed5b16a4-c282-11f1-8b11-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2JV49E.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ed5b16a4-c282-11f1-8b11-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2JV49E.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0aafc0c4-c283-11f1-8445-23721d23030c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 19:19:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ed5b16a4-c282-11f1-8b11-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2JV49E.jpg">© Manaure Quintero, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>What we know about espionage, treason allegations against Germany's ex-spy chief</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261007-what-we-know-about-espionage-treason-allegations-against-germany-s-ex-spy-chief</link><description>
A court on Wednesday ordered the former head of Germany's foreign intelligence service August Hanning to remain in pretrial detention after his arrest on suspicion of espionage and treason, along with a former deputy who allegedly supplied him with secret files. Here's what we know about one of the biggest security breaches in German history.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/498bd9a8-c257-11f1-bb2c-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25254411016248.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/498bd9a8-c257-11f1-bb2c-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25254411016248.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">60a7173a-c255-11f1-b4b7-ed2219ea2917</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 14:06:59 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/498bd9a8-c257-11f1-bb2c-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25254411016248.jpg">© Liesa Johannssen, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia warns against spreading 'false information' as reports emerge of second plague case</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261007-russia-warns-against-spreading-false-information-reports-emerge-second-plague-case</link><description>
The World Health Organization joined Western leaders on Wednesday in urging Russia to share more information about what killed a plague institute worker in Siberia as reports emerged of a second suspected case. The Kremlin said Moscow had shared what it knew and accused the media ​of spreading "false information".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/59435228-c24c-11f1-ac27-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26278372667862.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/59435228-c24c-11f1-ac27-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26278372667862.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a82b71d0-c24d-11f1-b60f-fd2056609791</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 13:43:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/59435228-c24c-11f1-ac27-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26278372667862.jpg">© AP, Handout Irkutsk Anti-Plague Research Institute of Siberia and Far East</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Nobel Prize in Chemistry awarded to France's Henri Kagan, Japan's Kenso Soai</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261007-nobel-prize-in-chemistry-jointly-awarded-to-france-s-henri-kagan-japan-s-kenso-soai</link><description>
Henri Kagan and Kenso Soai were jointly awarded the Nobel Prize in Chemistry for solving a 100-year-old chemical mystery, the Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences said on Wednesday. Nobel Prize recipients receive a prize of 12 million Swedish kronor (about $1.2 million).  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d7b6b2b0-c235-11f1-b100-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2GL6EG.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d7b6b2b0-c235-11f1-b100-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2GL6EG.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">30ab003c-c228-11f1-9111-d3268635940b</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 09:52:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d7b6b2b0-c235-11f1-b100-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2GL6EG.jpg">© Jonathan Nackstrand, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Politkovskaya 'predicted' Russia's turn under Putin, editor says on 20th anniversary of her death</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261007-anna-politkovskaya-the-slain-reporter-who-predicted-russia-future</link><description>
Assassinated Russian journalist Anna Politkovskaya "predicted" Moscow's trajectory under President Vladimir Putin 20 years ago,  her former editor said ahead of the anniversary of her death on Wednesday. Politkovskaya had reported on the war in Chechnya and Putin's rise before she was gunned down in her Moscow apartment block on October 7, 2006.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f785f036-c223-11f1-acd5-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23318667254630.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f785f036-c223-11f1-acd5-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23318667254630.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c0921dc0-c223-11f1-ab67-95927788547b</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 08:32:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f785f036-c223-11f1-acd5-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23318667254630.jpg">© Pavel Golovkin, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia launches one of its biggest strikes on Ukraine, killing at least 21 civilians</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261007-at-least-two-killed-in-fire-caused-by-massive-strikes-on-kyiv</link><description>
Russian missiles and drones killed at least 21 people in Ukraine, including four children, in what President Volodymyr Zelensky ‌called a “massive” strike on Wednesday. Ukraine has come under increased attack in recent weeks as Russian attacks have targeted energy infrastructure and rail and road transport.   
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8bc7294e-c211-11f1-8aec-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-07T053758Z-164245437-RC22YNA4P69K-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8bc7294e-c211-11f1-8aec-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-07T053758Z-164245437-RC22YNA4P69K-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b4a2f570-c20f-11f1-be00-9d3dece0adb8</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 05:56:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8bc7294e-c211-11f1-8aec-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-07T053758Z-164245437-RC22YNA4P69K-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg">© Vladyslav Sodel, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Trump says will speak with Putin over Russia's reported plague death</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-trump-says-he-will-speak-to-putin-over-reported-plague-death-in-russia</link><description>
US President Donald Trump said Tuesday he would speak “very soon” with Russian President Vladimir Putin over the reported death from plague of a laboratory technician, as Washington and the World Health Organization pressed Moscow for greater transparency and clarity over conflicting accounts of the incident in Siberia.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/35f3ab30-c16e-11f1-8701-73f176a2394c/w:1024/p:16x9/0d9752045f8fa082683fe0099656b7298c90813f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/35f3ab30-c16e-11f1-8701-73f176a2394c/w:1024/p:16x9/0d9752045f8fa082683fe0099656b7298c90813f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">83da361a-c1d8-11f1-aee6-5f1a754fd3d8</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 22:51:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/35f3ab30-c16e-11f1-8701-73f176a2394c/w:1024/p:16x9/0d9752045f8fa082683fe0099656b7298c90813f.jpg">© Igor Ivanko, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Germany's former spy chief detained on suspicion of trading state secrets</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-former-german-spy-chief-detained-over-suspected-treasonous-espionage</link><description>
Former German spy chief August Hanning was detained Tuesday on suspicion of treason and espionage after prosecutors accused him of paying for secret intelligence documents and using them to prepare an analysis for a foreign intelligence service, in a case that could strain Berlin’s ties with allied spy agencies.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95531a82-c189-11f1-8815-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/91a7ef13c7a16e3d52ad91fa615eb093b8a68a0f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95531a82-c189-11f1-8815-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/91a7ef13c7a16e3d52ad91fa615eb093b8a68a0f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a6a68898-c1cd-11f1-886a-5fc42d75ec39</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 21:34:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95531a82-c189-11f1-8815-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/91a7ef13c7a16e3d52ad91fa615eb093b8a68a0f.jpg">© Abdelhak Senna, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Russian lab worker's death sparks plague fears as unverified claims spread online</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261006-russian-lab-worker-s-death-sparks-plague-fears-as-unverified-claims-spread-online-1</link><description>
The death of a 28-year-old Russian lab worker at Siberia's Irkutsk Anti-Plague Research Institute has sparked online panic about a "plague, despite the WHO assessing the public health risk in Russia as low. Unverified claims about how the worker became ill, including a laboratory accident involving a test tube, are circulating online. Misleading posts and out-of-context videos have also fuelled speculation and fear. Vedika Bahl goes through them, and what we know, in Truth or Fake.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/45f2fbf0-c1c6-11f1-be56-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12002312286ac55cea366708-19046261.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/45f2fbf0-c1c6-11f1-be56-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12002312286ac55cea366708-19046261.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fc75c5fc-c1c5-11f1-bd68-fb988e5cfdc5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 20:58:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Police make seventh arrest over UK airbase incident</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/police-make-seventh-arrest-over-uk-airbase-incident</link><description>
A seventh man was arrested Tuesday over a major incident last month at a British military airbase used by the United States to launch strikes on Iran, police said. The arrest came a day after President Donald Trump said the United States had withdrawn all B-1 bombers from RAF Fairford because of "threats" he believed were linked to Tehran. A 22-year-old British male was arrested in London "on suspicion of preparation of terrorist acts", Britain's Counter-Terrorism Policing network said in a statement. Six men in their 20s have already been arrested and released on bail after three suspicious vans were stopped near the base in southwest England on September 27. FRANCE 24's Bénédicte Paviot reports from London.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0355f7dc-c1be-11f1-9453-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-203840-204355-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0355f7dc-c1be-11f1-9453-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261006-203840-204355-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0872f008-c1be-11f1-902a-15b8d05e51cb</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 19:51:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>German ex-spy chief arrested for suspected espionage, treason</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/german-ex-spy-chief-arrested-for-suspected-espionage-treason</link><description>
A former German spy chief was arrested Tuesday on suspicion of espionage and treason, an embarrassing case at a time when the country is seeking to broaden the powers of its intelligence agencies. August Hanning, who ran Germany's BND foreign intelligence agency from 1998 to 2005, is accused of espionage, treason and working for foreign intelligence services, federal prosecutors said. FRANCE 24's Nick Holdsworth reports from Berlin.
