Bulgarian authorities on Tuesday launched a search for missing crew members of a boat that sank in its economic zone in the Black Sea after drones hit two merchant vessels. Black Sea shipping has been hit by growing fallout from the war in Ukraine in recent months. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25bea9ca-c170-11f1-93bd-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/13908dac13d542b51b3d44201a660a727f65fdd9.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25bea9ca-c170-11f1-93bd-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/13908dac13d542b51b3d44201a660a727f65fdd9.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">27219ca0-c170-11f1-99f9-ff4b5e6c188a</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 10:24:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25bea9ca-c170-11f1-93bd-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/13908dac13d542b51b3d44201a660a727f65fdd9.jpg">© Stringer, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukraine hits Moscow with one of its largest drone attacks in two years</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261006-massive-ukrainian-drone-attack-targets-moscow-russian-officials-say</link><description>
